:[0.7322,1.6982,2.6236,1.9883,2.2422,2.3232,2.0833,3.1404,0.0888]}]},"called_by":"prosecution"}},{"t":1794815425.577668,"role":"prosecution","kind":"charge","data":{"sin":"other","exhibits":["EX-1"],"argument":"The strategy exhibits significant performance degradation in the holdout period, with the Sharpe ratio dropping from 1.91 to 0.36, indicating severe overfitting to the research sample."}},{"t":1794815432.84758,"role":"defence","kind":"rebuttal","data":{"sin":"other","concede":false,"exhibits":["EX-1","EX-2","EX-3","EX-4"],"argument":"The performance gap in the holdout period is primarily due to the introduction of a 10 bps cost assumption and a mandatory lag in the test, whereas the research Sharpe is robust across regimes (EX-4) and free from look-ahead bias (EX-2). Given the high probability of a positive true Sharpe (EX-3), the strategy remains viable despite the conservative holdout parameters."}},{"t":1794815439.6027465,"role":"judge","kind":"verdict","data":{"ruling":"paper","findings":[{"sin":"other","sustained":true,"exhibits":["EX-1"],"struck":false}],"capital_allowed":0.0,"opinion":"The strategy shows a significant performance collapse in the holdout period (EX-1), where the Sharpe ratio drops from 1.91 to 0.36. While the research-period performance appears robust against look-ahead bias (EX-2) and trial-selection bias (EX-3), the massive discrepancy in the holdout test suggests the strategy is overfitted to the specific research sample. The rebuttal correctly notes that the holdout test included stricter cost and lag assumptions, but the magnitude of the degradation is too large to ignore. Therefore, the strategy is relegated to paper trading to verify if it can maintain a positive edge under live market conditions before committing real capital.","unsupported":false,"defaulted":false}}],"calls":7,"tokens_in":10624,"tokens_out":441,"seconds":323.744}